export const dbConfigStructuralDocsPages = {
  "dbconfig-overview-engine": {
    "id": "dbconfig-overview-engine",
    "title": "9.1: DB Config Architecture & Decision Engine (getConfigLevel)",
    "title_hi": "9.1: DB Config Architecture aur getConfigLevel() Decision Engine",
    "subtitle": "How Maximo evaluates staged configuration records in ConfigureService.java to decide between Live Refresh and Admin Mode.",
    "subtitle_hi": "ConfigureService.java kaise staged changes evaluate karta hai aur Live Refresh ya Admin Mode decide karta hai.",
    "html": "<h1>9.1: DB Config Architecture & Decision Engine (getConfigLevel)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">How Maximo evaluates staged configuration records in ConfigureService.java to decide between Live Refresh and Admin Mode.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. Overview &amp; Core Architecture</h2>\n  <p>In IBM Maximo, when changes are made in the <strong>Database Configuration</strong> application, they are initially staged in configuration tables (<code>MAXOBJECTCFG</code>, <code>MAXATTRIBUTECFG</code>, <code>MAXTABLECFG</code>, <code>MAXSYSINDEXES</code>, etc.) with a change status (<code>CHANGED</code> column).</p>\n  <p>When the user clicks <strong>\"Apply Configuration Changes\"</strong> (or runs <code>configdb</code>), Maximo's <code>psdi.app.configure.ConfigureService</code> evaluates the staged changes to determine the <strong>Configuration Level</strong>:</p>\n\n  <h3>Configuration Level Constants (ConfigureServiceRemote.java)</h3>\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n    <div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>ConfigureServiceRemote.java</span></div>\n    <pre>public static final int CONFIGDB_NONE      = 0; // No changes to configure\npublic static final int CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT = 1; // Non-Structural Change (Live Refresh / No Admin Mode required)\npublic static final int CONFIGDB_STRUCT    = 2; // Structural Change (Admin Mode mandatory / Full configdb required)</pre>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>2. Decision Engine: ConfigureService.getConfigLevel()</h2>\n  <p>The method <code>getConfigLevel(UserInfo ui)</code> in <code>psdi.app.configure.ConfigureService</code> is the single source of truth that inspects all staged records and returns <code>0</code>, <code>1</code>, or <code>2</code>.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n    <div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Decision Flowchart</span></div>\n    <pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    Start[\"Database Configuration Triggered\"] --&gt; CheckChanged{\"Any MAXOBJECTCFG where changed != 'N'?\"}\n    \n    CheckChanged -- No --&gt; CheckIndexes{\"Any MAXSYSINDEXES where changed != 'N'?\"}\n    CheckIndexes -- Yes --&gt; Level1[\"CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (Level 1)&lt;br/&gt;• Live Refresh without Admin Mode\"]\n    CheckIndexes -- No --&gt; Level0[\"CONFIGDB_NONE (Level 0)&lt;br/&gt;• Nothing to configure\"]\n    \n    CheckChanged -- Yes --&gt; CheckMassRebuild{\"changed = 'M'?\"}\n    CheckMassRebuild -- Yes --&gt; Level2[\"CONFIGDB_STRUCT (Level 2)&lt;br/&gt;• Admin Mode Mandatory\"]\n    \n    CheckMassRebuild -- No --&gt; CheckNonPersistentOnly{\"Only Non-Persistent Objects&lt;br/&gt;(persistent = 0)?\"}\n    CheckNonPersistentOnly -- Yes --&gt; Level1\n    \n    CheckNonPersistentOnly -- No --&gt; CheckTableDrop{\"changed = 'R' on persistent table&lt;br/&gt;(except Audit tables)?\"}\n    CheckTableDrop -- Yes --&gt; Level2\n    \n    CheckTableDrop -- No --&gt; LoopObjects[\"Loop through each modified Object &amp; its Attributes\"]\n    LoopObjects --&gt; CheckObjType{\"Table changed is 'I' or 'R'?\"}\n    CheckObjType -- \"Yes &amp; isAuditTable = false\" --&gt; Level2\n    CheckObjType -- \"Yes &amp; isAuditTable = true\" --&gt; CheckAttrLevel\n    CheckObjType -- \"No (changed = 'Y')\" --&gt; CheckObjectFields{\"Any field changed outside the 5 safe fields?\"}\n    \n    CheckObjectFields -- Yes --&gt; Level2\n    CheckObjectFields -- No --&gt; CheckAttrLevel[\"Check Attributes in MAXATTRIBUTECFG\"]\n    \n    CheckAttrLevel --&gt; CheckNewDeletedAttr{\"New Attribute ('I') or Deleted Attribute ('R')?\"}\n    CheckNewDeletedAttr -- Yes --&gt; Level2\n    CheckNewDeletedAttr -- No --&gt; CheckModifiedAttrs{\"Modified Attribute Fields Check\"}\n    \n    CheckModifiedAttrs -- \"LENGTH, SCALE, MAXTYPE, REQUIRED, PERSISTENT, COLUMNNAME, TEXT Search\" --&gt; Level2\n    CheckModifiedAttrs -- \"TITLE, REMARKS, DOMAINID, DEFAULTVALUE, ESIG, AUTOKEY, CLASSNAME\" --&gt; Level1</pre>\n  </div>\n</section>",
    "html_hi": "<h1>9.1: DB Config Architecture aur getConfigLevel() Decision Engine</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">ConfigureService.java kaise staged changes evaluate karta hai aur Live Refresh ya Admin Mode decide karta hai.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. Overview aur Core Architecture</h2>\n  <p>Maximo Database Configuration app me jab koi changes kiye jaate hain, toh woh pehle staging tables (<code>MAXOBJECTCFG</code>, <code>MAXATTRIBUTECFG</code>, <code>MAXSYSINDEXES</code>) me stage hote hain.</p>\n  <p>Jab user <strong>\"Apply Configuration Changes\"</strong> par click karta hai, toh <code>psdi.app.configure.ConfigureService</code> evaluate karke <strong>Configuration Level (0, 1, ya 2)</strong> decide karta hai:</p>\n\n  <h3>Configuration Level Constants</h3>\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n    <div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Java Constants</span></div>\n    <pre>public static final int CONFIGDB_NONE      = 0; // Koi change nahi hai\npublic static final int CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT = 1; // Non-Structural Change (Live Refresh / Bina Admin Mode ke)\npublic static final int CONFIGDB_STRUCT    = 2; // Structural Change (Admin Mode mandatory / Full configdb zaroori)</pre>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>2. Decision Engine (ConfigureService.getConfigLevel)</h2>\n  <p><code>getConfigLevel()</code> method pure staging dictionary ko scan karta hai aur check karta hai ki physical schema alter hoga ya sirf metadata refresh hoga.</p>\n</section>"
  },
  "dbconfig-structural-changes": {
    "id": "dbconfig-structural-changes",
    "title": "9.2: Structural Changes (Level 2 & Mandatory Admin Mode)",
    "title_hi": "9.2: Structural Changes (Level 2 aur Mandatory Admin Mode)",
    "subtitle": "Operations that alter physical tables, columns, data types, lengths, or storage partitions.",
    "subtitle_hi": "Physical database schema, tables, columns, length aur data types ko modify karne wale structural changes.",
    "html": "<h1>9.2: Structural Changes (Level 2 & Mandatory Admin Mode)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Operations that alter physical tables, columns, data types, lengths, or storage partitions.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. What is a Structural Change (CONFIGDB_STRUCT = 2)?</h2>\n  <p>A change is classified as <strong>Structural</strong> if it alters the physical schema (DDL), storage characteristics, data integrity constraints, or table identity of the underlying database. These changes strictly require <strong>Admin Mode</strong> to be enabled.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Object / Table Level Triggers</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Adding a New Persistent Table:</strong> Creating a new object where <code>changed = 'I'</code> and <code>persistent = 1</code> (excluding Audit tables).</li>\n    <li><strong>Deleting an Existing Persistent Table:</strong> Dropping an object where <code>changed = 'R'</code> and <code>persistent = 1</code> (excluding Audit tables).</li>\n    <li><strong>Mass Rebuild Marker:</strong> Objects marked with <code>changed = 'M'</code>.</li>\n    <li><strong>Modifying Critical Object Properties:</strong>\n      <ul>\n        <li><code>STORAGEPARTITION</code> (Moving table to a different tablespace/storage partition).</li>\n        <li><code>ENTITYNAME</code> / <code>OBJECTNAME</code> (Renaming physical table or object mapping).</li>\n        <li><code>ISVIEW</code> (Converting a Table to a View or vice versa).</li>\n        <li><code>EXTENDSOBJECT</code> (Changing object inheritance hierarchy).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>3. Attribute / Column Level Triggers</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Adding a New Attribute:</strong> Staged with <code>CHANGED = 'I'</code> (requires <code>ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN</code>).</li>\n    <li><strong>Deleting an Existing Attribute:</strong> Staged with <code>CHANGED = 'R'</code> or <code>'D'</code>.</li>\n    <li><strong>Physical Column Property Changes:</strong>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong><code>LENGTH</code>:</strong> Increasing or decreasing column character/numeric length.</li>\n        <li><strong><code>SCALE</code>:</strong> Modifying decimal places.</li>\n        <li><strong><code>MAXTYPE</code>:</strong> Changing data type (e.g. <code>ALN</code> to <code>UPPER</code>, <code>INTEGER</code> to <code>BIGINT</code>, <code>AMOUNT</code>, <code>DATETIME</code>).</li>\n        <li><strong><code>PERSISTENT</code>:</strong> Toggling attribute between Persistent and Non-Persistent.</li>\n        <li><strong><code>REQUIRED</code>:</strong> Adding or removing physical <code>NOT NULL</code> constraint.</li>\n        <li><strong><code>COLUMNNAME</code>:</strong> Renaming the physical database column.</li>\n        <li><strong><code>SEARCHTYPE = 'TEXT'</code>:</strong> Enabling native database text search indexes.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </li>\n  </ul>\n</section>",
    "html_hi": "<h1>9.2: Structural Changes (Level 2 aur Mandatory Admin Mode)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Physical database schema, tables, columns, length aur data types ko modify karne wale structural changes.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. Structural Change Kya Hota Hai (Level 2)?</h2>\n  <p>Jab kisi change ki wajah se database ka physical schema (DDL), column data types, table drop/recreate, ya storage partition alter hota hai, toh Maximo use <strong>Structural Change (Level 2)</strong> mark karta hai aur iske liye <strong>Admin Mode</strong> mandatory hota hai.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Kaunse Changes Structural Hote Hain?</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>New Persistent Table Add/Delete:</strong> Naya persistent MBO create karna ya drop karna.</li>\n    <li><strong>New Column / Attribute:</strong> Naya attribute add karna (<code>ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN</code>).</li>\n    <li><strong>Length / Scale / Data Type:</strong> Column length badhana/ghatana ya data type change karna (jaise <code>ALN</code> se <code>UPPER</code>).</li>\n    <li><strong>Required / Not Null:</strong> Physical <code>NOT NULL</code> constraint lagana ya hatana.</li>\n    <li><strong>Storage Partition:</strong> Table ko dusre tablespace me move karna.</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
  },
  "dbconfig-nonstructural-changes": {
    "id": "dbconfig-nonstructural-changes",
    "title": "9.3: Non-Structural Changes & Live Refresh (Level 1)",
    "title_hi": "9.3: Non-Structural Changes aur Live Refresh (Level 1)",
    "subtitle": "Metadata-only changes executed instantly at runtime without Admin Mode or server downtime.",
    "subtitle_hi": "Bina Admin Mode ya server downtime ke metadata refresh ke zariye turant apply hone wale changes.",
    "html": "<h1>9.3: Non-Structural Changes & Live Refresh (Level 1)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Metadata-only changes executed instantly at runtime without Admin Mode or server downtime.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. What is a Non-Structural Change (CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT = 1)?</h2>\n  <p>A change is classified as <strong>Non-Structural</strong> if it only affects Maximo Data Dictionary metadata (<code>MAXOBJECT</code>, <code>MAXATTRIBUTE</code>, <code>MAXSYSINDEXES</code>) and application runtime behavior without requiring destructive database schema alterations or table locks.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Safe Object-Level Fields (The 5 Safe Fields)</h2>\n  <p>In <code>MAXOBJECTCFG</code>, changing only these 5 properties is strictly Non-Structural:</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li><strong><code>DESCRIPTION</code>:</strong> Human-readable label/description of the object.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>ESIGFILTER</code>:</strong> Electronic signature filter condition.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>EAUDITFILTER</code>:</strong> Electronic audit condition filter.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>EAUDITENABLED</code>:</strong> Toggling Audit on/off.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>EAUDITTBNAME</code>:</strong> Audit table name specification (e.g., <code>A_WORKORDER</code>).</li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h2>3. Safe Attribute-Level Fields</h2>\n  <p>In <code>MAXATTRIBUTECFG</code>, modifying existing attributes on these fields is Non-Structural:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong><code>TITLE</code>:</strong> UI label/title of the attribute.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>REMARKS</code>:</strong> Help/description text.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>DOMAINID</code>:</strong> Attaching, changing, or detaching a Domain (ALN, NUMERIC, SYNONYM, TABLE, CROSSOVER).</li>\n    <li><strong><code>DEFAULTVALUE</code>:</strong> Changing default value populated in UI/MBO layer.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>ESIGENABLED</code>:</strong> Enabling/disabling Electronic Signature requirement.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>CANAUTONUM</code> / <code>AUTOKEYNAME</code>:</strong> Enabling auto-numbering and selecting autokey seed.</li>\n    <li><strong><code>CLASSNAME</code>:</strong> Setting or changing MboValueAdapter validation class (valid class must exist in classpath).</li>\n    <li><strong><code>SEARCHTYPE</code>:</strong> Switching between <code>EXACT</code>, <code>WILDCARD</code>, and <code>NONE</code> (except <code>TEXT</code>).</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>",
    "html_hi": "<h1>9.3: Non-Structural Changes aur Live Refresh (Level 1)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Bina Admin Mode ya server downtime ke metadata refresh ke zariye turant apply hone wale changes.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>1. Non-Structural Changes Kya Hote Hain?</h2>\n  <p>Non-Structural changes sirf Maximo Data Dictionary (<code>MAXOBJECT</code>, <code>MAXATTRIBUTE</code>) ke metadata ko update karte hain. Inhe apply karne ke liye Admin Mode ki zaroorat nahi hoti aur yeh <strong>Live Refresh</strong> ke zariye bina downtime ke live apply ho jaate hain.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Safe 5 Object Fields</h2>\n  <p><code>MAXOBJECTCFG</code> me sirf in 5 fields ka change Non-Structural hota hai:</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li><code>DESCRIPTION</code></li>\n    <li><code>ESIGFILTER</code></li>\n    <li><code>EAUDITFILTER</code></li>\n    <li><code>EAUDITENABLED</code></li>\n    <li><code>EAUDITTBNAME</code></li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h2>3. Safe Attribute Fields</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Domain Attachment:</strong> ALN, SYNONYM, ya Table Domain attach/detach karna (<code>DOMAINID</code>).</li>\n    <li><strong>Title &amp; Remarks:</strong> Field ka label ya description badalna.</li>\n    <li><strong>Default Value:</strong> MBO default value set karna.</li>\n    <li><strong>Auto-numbering:</strong> Autokey seed attach karna (<code>AUTOKEYNAME</code>).</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
  },
  "dbconfig-special-exceptions": {
    "id": "dbconfig-special-exceptions",
    "title": "9.4: 7 Specialized Exceptions & Complete Comparison Matrix",
    "title_hi": "9.4: 7 Specialized Exceptions aur Comparison Matrix",
    "subtitle": "E-Audit table creation, live secondary indexes, non-persistent objects, text search, and comparison matrix.",
    "subtitle_hi": "E-Audit tables, secondary indexes, non-persistent objects, aur structural vs non-structural ka complete matrix.",
    "html": "<h1>9.4: 7 Specialized Exceptions & Complete Comparison Matrix</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">E-Audit table creation, live secondary indexes, non-persistent objects, text search, and comparison matrix.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>7 Special Cases &amp; Exceptions in ConfigureService.java</h2>\n  \n  <h3>Exception 1: E-Audit Enablement (A_tablename) — Live Table Creation without Admin Mode</h3>\n  <p>When you enable E-Audit on an object (e.g., <code>WORKORDER</code>), Maximo creates a physical audit table (e.g., <code>A_WORKORDER</code>) in the database. Despite creating a physical table, Maximo classifies this as <strong>Non-Structural (<code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT = 1</code>)</strong>.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Why?</strong> The base table (<code>WORKORDER</code>) is never altered or locked, zero data backup/restore is needed, and auditing is handled at the MBO application layer (<code>Mbo.save()</code>).</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Exception 2: Secondary Indexes (MAXSYSINDEXES) — Live Index DDL</h3>\n  <p>Creating or dropping custom secondary indexes in the Indexes tab without modifying table columns runs live in the background (<code>CREATE INDEX</code> / <code>DROP INDEX</code>) without Admin Mode (<strong>Level 1</strong>).</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 3: Non-Persistent Objects &amp; Attributes (persistent = 0)</h3>\n  <p>Creating new Non-Persistent Objects or adding Non-Persistent Attributes is strictly <strong>Non-Structural (Level 1)</strong> because they exist solely in Java memory / MBO framework without any physical database footprint.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 4: Multi-Tenant Extension Views (V_tenant_tablename)</h3>\n  <p>Tenant extension views are created/updated live via <code>applyTenantChanges()</code> without requiring Admin Mode across tenants.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 5: SEARCHTYPE Exception (EXACT/WILDCARD vs TEXT)</h3>\n  <p>Switching between <code>EXACT</code>, <code>WILDCARD</code>, and <code>NONE</code> is Level 1. Switching to or from <code>TEXT</code> escalates to <strong>Level 2 (Structural)</strong> because it requires building native database text search indexes.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 6: CLASSNAME Escalation</h3>\n  <p>If the Java class exists in the classpath $\rightarrow$ <strong>Level 1</strong>. If <code>ClassNotFoundException</code> occurs $\rightarrow$ escalated to <strong>Level 2</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 7: Language Tables (L_tablename)</h3>\n  <p>Unlike Audit tables, Multi-Language tables (<code>L_table</code>) are <strong>Structural (Level 2)</strong> and require Admin Mode because multi-language modifies base table attribute flags (<code>MLINUSE</code>) and key constraints.</p>\n\n  <h2>Comprehensive Comparison Matrix</h2>\n  <table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th>Scenario / Operation</th>\n        <th>Database Objects Affected</th>\n        <th>Configuration Level</th>\n        <th>Admin Mode Required?</th>\n        <th>Execution Mechanism</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>E-Audit Enabled (A_table)</strong></td>\n        <td>New Audit Table (<code>A_table</code>)</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Live <code>CREATE TABLE</code> &amp; index creation via <code>ConfigDBThread</code></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Secondary Index Add/Drop</strong></td>\n        <td>Database Index</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Live <code>CREATE INDEX</code> / <code>DROP INDEX</code> DDL</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Non-Persistent Add/Modify</strong></td>\n        <td>Maximo Metadata only</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Maximo Data Dictionary (<code>MAXIMODD</code>) reload</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Attribute Domain / Default</strong></td>\n        <td>Maximo Metadata only</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Metadata refresh &amp; cache reload</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Attribute Label / Remarks</strong></td>\n        <td>Maximo Metadata only</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Metadata refresh &amp; cache reload</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Attribute ClassName (Valid)</strong></td>\n        <td>Maximo Metadata only</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Class validated via JVM classloader</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>SearchType (EXACT / WILDCARD)</strong></td>\n        <td>Maximo Metadata only</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_NONSTRUCT (1)</code></td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Query logic updated in MBO framework</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>SearchType (TEXT)</strong></td>\n        <td>Native Text Index</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_STRUCT (2)</code></td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Text Search index engine build</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Language Table (L_table)</strong></td>\n        <td>New Language Table (<code>L_table</code>)</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_STRUCT (2)</code></td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Full table creation &amp; ML relationship bind</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Column Length / Type / Scale</strong></td>\n        <td>Physical Table Schema</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_STRUCT (2)</code></td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Full table backup, drop, recreate, restore</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Add / Drop Column</strong></td>\n        <td>Physical Table Schema</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_STRUCT (2)</code></td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td><code>ALTER TABLE</code> / full table recreate</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Move Tablespace (Storage Partition)</strong></td>\n        <td>Physical Storage</td>\n        <td><code>CONFIGDB_STRUCT (2)</code></td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Full table recreate on target tablespace</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</section>",
    "html_hi": "<h1>9.4: 7 Specialized Exceptions aur Comparison Matrix</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">E-Audit tables, secondary indexes, non-persistent objects, aur structural vs non-structural ka complete matrix.</p>\n\n<section>\n  <h2>7 Special Exceptions in Maximo ConfigureService</h2>\n  \n  <h3>Exception 1: E-Audit Enablement (A_tablename)</h3>\n  <p>Jab aap kisi table par E-Audit enable karte hain toh database me physical <code>A_tablename</code> create hoti hai. Iske bawajood Maximo ise <strong>Non-Structural (Level 1)</strong> manta hai kyunki base table alter nahi hoti.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 2: Secondary Indexes (Live Index DDL)</h3>\n  <p>Indexes tab me naya index add/drop karna bina Admin Mode ke live execute hota hai (Level 1).</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 3: Non-Persistent Entities</h3>\n  <p>Non-Persistent objects aur attributes database me exist nahi karte, isliye yeh hamesha Level 1 hote hain.</p>\n\n  <h3>Exception 4: SEARCHTYPE TEXT Exception</h3>\n  <p>EXACT aur WILDCARD Level 1 hain, lekin TEXT search database text index build karta hai isliye Level 2 hai.</p>\n\n  <h2>Comparison Matrix Summary</h2>\n  <table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th>Operation</th>\n        <th>Level</th>\n        <th>Admin Mode?</th>\n        <th>Mechanism</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>E-Audit Table (A_table)</strong></td>\n        <td>Level 1</td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Live CREATE TABLE</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Secondary Indexes</strong></td>\n        <td>Level 1</td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Live Index DDL</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Domain / Default Value</strong></td>\n        <td>Level 1</td>\n        <td>❌ No</td>\n        <td>Metadata Refresh</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Column Length / Type / Scale</strong></td>\n        <td>Level 2</td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Full Table Rebuild / ALTER</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td><strong>Language Table (L_table)</strong></td>\n        <td>Level 2</td>\n        <td>✅ Yes</td>\n        <td>Full ML Table Creation</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</section>"
  }
};
